<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-16629] Wrong calculation of replies count for queries with partition pruning and enabled parallelism</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-16629</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently a simple query is freezing forever if query parallelism is enabled and partition pruning extracts more than one partition. This caused by wrong replies count estimation made on a reducer node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The problematic query looks like this: &lt;tt&gt;select * from t where aff_key in (&apos;a&apos;, &apos;b&apos;, &apos;c&apos;)&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please note that field &lt;em&gt;aff_key&lt;/em&gt; should be an affinity key and be a part of the compound PK.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
